/-
# Dregg2.Circuit.CustomDeployedBytePin — the DEPLOYED custom descriptor, pinned AT ITS BYTES.

## Why this file exists

Every prior Lean statement about `Effect::Custom` was about a Lean OBJECT (`customV3`,
`customProofBind`, `demoC`) whose only tie to the shipped artifact was PROSE plus a CI shell script
(`scripts/check-descriptor-drift.sh`, which needs a full `lake build` and regenerates the whole
registry). No `#guard emitVmJson2` golden existed for ANY rotation-v3 registry member — the
per-descriptor byte pins the tree uses everywhere else stop at the by-name predicate surface.

This file closes that for the ONE member that carries the recursion `proofBind` op: it pins
`withDfaRcPins (gentianDeployedBareRefuse customV3)` — the exact composition
`EmitRotationV3.lean` prints for key `customVmDescriptor2R24` — to the exact bytes committed at
`circuit/descriptors/rotation-v3-staged-registry.tsv` line 19, column 3, which Rust reads by
`include_str!` + tab scan (`effect_vm_descriptors.rs::V3_STAGED_REGISTRY_TSV`).

**Consequence.** Statements below are about the DEPLOYED BYTES, not about a Lean mirror of them.
That is the (c) rung; `CustomApex` / `CustomCarrierAttack` / `CustomLeafEncoding` all sit at (a)/(b).

## What is pinned, and what is proved

`#guard`s (the tree's byte-pin idiom, evaluated not kernel-checked):
  * `emitVmJson2 deployedCustomV3 == CUSTOM_V3_DEPLOYED_GOLDEN` — THE BYTE PIN.
  * the deployed registry's member for the key emits the SAME bytes (so `deployedCustomV3` IS the
    registry member, not a look-alike).
  * the committed bytes contain EXACTLY ONE `proof_bind` op, and its JSON is EXACTLY
    `{"t":"proof_bind","guard":{"t":"var","v":8},"commit":{"t":"var","v":72},"vk":{"t":"var","v":68}}`.
  * the committed bytes mention NO commitment / VK column (72..75, `CUSTOM_COMMIT_TEETH_COL`+0..3,
    68..71, `CUSTOM_VK_TEETH_COL`+0..3) inside any `gate` body — the `pi_binding` pins and the one
    vacuous `proof_bind` are the only constraints that name them. The teeth bases are spelled by the
    emitter's own constants and NEVER as numerals here: see the note above `customBindingCols`, and
    the graveyard of flag-day retypings at §3b.

Theorems (over the values the pins tie to those bytes):
  * `customProofBind_is_deployed_columns` — the op's columns are literally `(8, 72, 68)`.
  * `deployed_custom_proofBind_vacuous` — the DEPLOYED per-row denotation of that op is `True` for
    EVERY environment. The deployed AIR imposes nothing on the custom commitment or VK columns.
  * `deployed_forged_row_admitted` / `deployed_forged_row_rejected_by_staged` — the forged row
    (`commit = 999`, unbacked for `demoEngine`) at the DEPLOYED columns is ADMITTED by the deployed
    gate and REJECTED by the staged in-AIR verifier. This is `CustomCarrierAttack.
    deployed_admits_unbacked` lifted off the toy `demoC` columns onto the SHIPPED ones.
  * `deployed_honest_row_accepted_by_staged` — the honest row (`commit = 123`) passes BOTH, so the
    staged gate is not refusing everything (non-vacuity, positive polarity).

**What this does NOT claim.** It says nothing about whether the custom binding is enforced
ELSEWHERE. It is not: the enforcement is the per-turn recursion FOLD
(`circuit-prove/src/joint_turn_recursive.rs::prove_custom_binding_node_state_segmented`, modelled by
`CustomBindingFromFold`), which the deployed chain prover reaches only through
`RotatedParticipantLeg::carrier_witness = Some(CarrierWitness::Custom _)` — a PROVER-CHOSEN field.
A custom leg with `carrier_witness: None` takes `prove_descriptor_leaf_rotated_with_segment` (the
sanctioned re-exec rung, `ivc_turn_chain.rs`) and gets NO binding node. Nothing in the deployed AIR
bytes below, and nothing on the light-client verify path
(`verify_turn_chain_recursive_from_parts`: vk fingerprint + root STARK + exposed segment), forces
the fold arm. So the honest reading of these pins is: **the deployed descriptor DECLARES the custom
binding and CONSTRAINS nothing about it; whether it is bound is a property of which fold arm the
prover took, which the verifier cannot observe.**

## Axiom hygiene
`#assert_axioms` on every theorem. No `sorry`, no `native_decide`, no new floor carrier
(`demoEngine` is the in-tree toy engine — a concrete `Bool` carrier, not a crypto hypothesis).
-/
